{"id":"252e3d555a5c71c8","group":"62","path":"62/62-thm-ACA0-maximal-ideals.md","title":"ACA0 and Maximal Ideals of Countable Rings or Domains","display":"thm-ACA0-maximal-ideals — ACA0 and Maximal Ideals of Countable Rings or Domains","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)","book_abbrev":"62","label":"62-thm-ACA0-maximal-ideals","aliases":["62-thm-ACA0-maximal-ideals"],"display":"thm-ACA0-maximal-ideals — ACA0 and Maximal Ideals of Countable Rings or Domains","depends_on":["[[62-df-RCA0]]","[[62-df-ACA0]]","[[62-df-ring-ideal-principles]]","[[62-df-equivalence-over-base]]","[[62-thm-ACA0-equivalences]]"],"source":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Lemma III.5.4; Theorem III.5.5","source_pages":[116,117],"source_pdf_pages":[134,135]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"62"},{"key":"label","html":"62-thm-ACA0-maximal-ideals"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>62-thm-ACA0-maximal-ideals</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-ACA0-maximal-ideals — ACA0 and Maximal Ideals of Countable Rings or Domains"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dd5e8930337c8b20\" href=\"?note=dd5e8930337c8b20\" title=\"62-df-RCA0\">62-df-RCA0</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"35af454d9caa8c9d\" href=\"?note=35af454d9caa8c9d\" title=\"62-df-ACA0\">62-df-ACA0</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"adcc911744508593\" href=\"?note=adcc911744508593\" title=\"62-df-ring-ideal-principles\">62-df-ring-ideal-principles</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"781620ab41bfeebd\" href=\"?note=781620ab41bfeebd\" title=\"62-df-equivalence-over-base\">62-df-equivalence-over-base</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"eddcc3574973d5b4\" href=\"?note=eddcc3574973d5b4\" title=\"62-thm-ACA0-equivalences\">62-thm-ACA0-equivalences</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source","html":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Lemma III.5.4; Theorem III.5.5"},{"key":"source_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>116</span><span>117</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>134</span><span>135</span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RCA}_0,\\mathrm{ACA}_0\">\\(\\mathrm{RCA}_0,\\mathrm{ACA}_0\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"dd5e8930337c8b20\" href=\"?note=dd5e8930337c8b20\" title=\"62-df-RCA0\">62-df-RCA0</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"35af454d9caa8c9d\" href=\"?note=35af454d9caa8c9d\" title=\"62-df-ACA0\">62-df-ACA0</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MI},\\mathrm{MID}\">\\(\\mathrm{MI},\\mathrm{MID}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"adcc911744508593\" href=\"?note=adcc911744508593\" title=\"62-df-ring-ideal-principles\">62-df-ring-ideal-principles</a>，EquivOver 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"781620ab41bfeebd\" href=\"?note=781620ab41bfeebd\" title=\"62-df-equivalence-over-base\">62-df-equivalence-over-base</a>；反向目标见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"eddcc3574973d5b4\" href=\"?note=eddcc3574973d5b4\" title=\"62-thm-ACA0-equivalences\">62-thm-ACA0-equivalences</a> 的总函数值域原则。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ACA0\\text{-}maximal\\text{-}ideals}\\vdash\\;\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\mathrm{ACA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{MI}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0),\\\\\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\mathrm{ACA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{MID}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}ACA0\\text{-}maximal\\text{-}ideals}\\vdash\\;\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\mathrm{ACA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{MI}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0),\\\\\n&amp;\\operatorname{EquivOver}_{S_2}(\\mathrm{ACA}_0,\\{\\mathrm{MID}\\};\\mathrm{RCA}_0).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>正向依 III.5.4，在有限生成记录中判定加入下一个环元素会不会使 1 成为有限环线性组合。算术理解给这种判定，贪心保持真理想并使每个未加入的元素在商中可逆。MI⇒MID 直接成立。</p>\n<p>反向依 III.5.5，给 f，把有理多项式环 Q[xₙ:n∈N] 的分式局部化，允许的分母恰含有一个仅使用 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"x_{f(m)}\">\\(x_{f(m)}\\)</span> 的非零单项式。这个条件为 Σ⁰₁，以枚举拉回运算给可数整环的表示，不先形成 range(f)。其极大理想 M 满足 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)\">\\(n\\in\\operatorname{range}(f)\\)</span> 当且仅当对应的 xₙ 不属于 M；若 n 在值域中，xₙ 已可逆，反向由原书的分母单项式比较给出。Δ⁰₁ 理解形成值域，恢复 ACA₀。这里没有使用 Zorn 引理。</p>\n<p>来源：第二版（2009），Lemma III.5.4; Theorem III.5.5；纸面页 116, 117；PDF 页 134, 135。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"62-df-RCA0","status":"resolved","id":"dd5e8930337c8b20","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-RCA0]]","embed":false},{"target":"62-df-ACA0","status":"resolved","id":"35af454d9caa8c9d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-ACA0]]","embed":false},{"target":"62-df-ring-ideal-principles","status":"resolved","id":"adcc911744508593","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-ring-ideal-principles]]","embed":false},{"target":"62-df-equivalence-over-base","status":"resolved","id":"781620ab41bfeebd","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-equivalence-over-base]]","embed":false},{"target":"62-thm-ACA0-equival